# Target C p6 e6 m6 closure

For e=6, nu(T)<=7. Exact S7 enumeration gives 470 six-support orbits and 7830 support/multiplicity orbits: 2308 of profile (3,1,1,1,1,1) and 5522 of profile (2,2,1,1,1,1).

Using rank(P)=3 and generalized weights (d1,d2,d3)>=(2,4,5): two rank-2 empty-block spaces require support intersection at least 2; a rank-2/rank-1 pair requires intersection at least 2 or union at least 5; a rank-1/rank-1 pair requires intersection at least 2 or union at least 4. These necessary conditions eliminate all (2,2,1,1,1,1) cases and leave 32 assignments, 77 empty sextuples, all profile (3,1,1,1,1,1).

The full retained phase scan has 7776 phase configurations and 18711 phase/sextuple pairs. For U equal to the sum of the six empty-block constraint spaces, the exact mod-2 rank census is {5:36, 6:2989, 7:15686}. Hence rank_Q(U)>=rank_F2(U)>3 in every case, contradicting U<=P and rank(P)=3.

Therefore e=6,m=6 is empty. Any e=6 survivor must have m in {7,8}.